<title>USA: Guidant to buy back up to $175 mln in stock.</title>
<headline>Guidant to buy back up to $175 mln in stock.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guidant Corp said on Wednesday it will begin to buy back up to $175 million of its common shares over the next several years in the open market or in privately negotiated purchases.</p>
<p>The purpose of the stock repurchase program is to meet the needs of Guidant's employee and director stock option programs, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The timing and amount of the share repurchases will depend on market conditions, it said.</p>
<p>Guidant, a medical device manufacturer, has about 72.1 million shares outstanding. Shares of Guidant were trading up 1-3/8 to 45-3/4.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
